# Jolly Challenge — Frontend

Frontend-only React application for the Jolly coding challenge. No backend — all logic
and state run in the browser.

## Stack

| Layer | Choice |
| ----- | ------ |
| Framework | React 19 + TypeScript |
| Build | Vite |
| Routing | React Router |
| Styling | Tailwind CSS |
| Validation | Zod |
| Tests | Vitest + Testing Library |

## Folder structure

```
src/
  app/                   # App shell (providers)
  common/
    components/          # Shared UI components
    layouts/             # Root and app layouts
  modules/
    home/                # Starter module — replace/extend for the challenge
      pages/
      routes.ts
      __tests__/
  routes/
    index.tsx            # Central route wiring
  styles/
    index.css            # Tailwind + CSS variables
  __tests__/
    setup.ts             # Vitest setup
  main.tsx
```

## Module conventions

Each feature module under `src/modules/<name>/` follows the layout in
`.cursor/rules/spaghetti-checker.mdc`:

- `pages/` — one page component per file
- `components/` — one component per file
- `hooks/` — one hook per file
- `schemas/` — Zod schemas (one per file)
- `routes.ts` — re-exports pages only (no component bodies)
- `__tests__/` — all tests (never beside source)

## Scripts

| Command | Purpose |
| ------- | ------- |
| `npm run dev` | Start Vite dev server (port 5173) |
| `npm run build` | Typecheck + production build |
| `npm run test` | Run Vitest unit tests |
| `npm run lint` | ESLint |
| `npm run typecheck` | TypeScript |
| `npm run check:spaghetti` | Module layout checker |
| `npm run check:security` | Frontend security checker |
| `npm run knip` | Dead code / unused dependency scan |

## AI tooling

Cursor rules in `.cursor/rules/` and hooks in `.cursor/hooks/` mirror the setup from
`password.manager`, adapted for this single-app frontend repo. Quality gates are
defined in `.cursor/rules/quality-gating.mdc`.

## Routes (current)

| Path | Page | Module |
| ---- | ---- | ------ |
| `/` | Home | `home` |

Add new routes in `src/routes/index.tsx` and create matching modules under `src/modules/`.
